WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.571
Something odd? See exactly what Wattzup hears from the bike.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.613
The pulse icon in the app bar opens Diagnostics, right over the ride.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.711
It lists what Wattzup sees right now: the server and its viewers, the Bluetooth link

00:00:22.711 --> 00:00:23.852
and the device.

00:00:24.052 --> 00:00:28.639
The transport, the packet count, how long it's been live, the last update and the

00:00:28.639 --> 00:00:29.562
last error.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.791
Below them, the latest raw packets, straight from the packet log.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.287
Copy details puts all of it on the clipboard as plain text, ready for a bug report.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.280
If the server drops, the first row says so: Offline, retrying every two seconds.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.485
On a phone, the dialog fits the screen.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.886
What the tests prove: every notification from the bike is appended to the raw packet

00:01:12.886 --> 00:01:13.419
log.

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:17.594
And Copy details copies the values and the packets, nothing more.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.657
That is journey twelve. Wattzup turns an Echelon bike or treadmill into a live

00:01:24.657 --> 00:01:25.972
training display.
